{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 0.485 acc / 0.464 F1, while config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) was much weaker at 0.208 acc / 0.172 F1. RNA is clearly the dominant modality, but we have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA). Uncertainty: whether a learned, biologically-informed encoder (scVI) substantially outperforms linear PCA for downstream classification. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) makes the minimal single-variable change from our best baseline—swapping only the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and all other hyperparameters constant. It cleanly isolates the encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) it directly answers whether representation quality is a major performance lever, which would inform every subsequent multimodal and multiprofile experiment; (2) if scVI is markedly better, we gain a stronger RNA backbone to build on; if similar, PCA suffices and we can focus budget on profile/aggregation/fusion axes; (3) it avoids conflating multiple design choices, keeping the comparison interpretable under a tight budget."
}

